[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m 3) reasoning (MANDATORY — INTERLEAVED NATURAL + SYNTACTIC)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m ================================================================================
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - "reasoning" MUST be a list of strings.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Each entry MUST be exactly 1 sentence and end with a period.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Reasoning MUST be interleaved:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     Odd-numbered entries: Natural-language reasoning.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     Even-numbered entries: Syntactic reasoning step (Z3-like statement).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Natural-language entries should explain the deduction in plain English.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Syntactic entries should encode the *newly deduced fact* as a Z3-like statement.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Tokens in Syntactic entries should encode the *mapped* to values in "attribute_values".
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m Syntactic entry format:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Every syntactic entry MUST start with "S<k>: " and MUST end with a period.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - <k> starts at 1 and increments by 1 for each syntactic step only (S1, S2, S3,...).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - The syntactic constraint MUST be solver-verifiable and may use ONLY:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   ==,!=, <, >, + d ==, Not(...), And(...), Or(...)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Each syntactic step MUST be written in the exact form: S<k>
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   Atomic operators:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     ==        (same house / equivalence)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m    !=        (not the same house)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     <         (somewhere to the left of)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     >         (somewhere to the right of)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     + d ==    (directed distance; d is a positive integer)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     == H      (fixed house index; H is an integer in 1..n_houses)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   Boolean operators:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     Not(e)    (negation of a single atomic expression)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     And(e1, e2,..., en)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     Or(e1, e2,..., en)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Boolean operators may ONLY be applied to valid atomic expressions.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m - Nested Boolean expressions are allowed but MUST remain solver-verifiable.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m Examples of valid INTERLEVED reasoning steps:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     The engineer is assigned to house 2.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     S1: engineer == 2.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     Since the engineer occupies house 2, the dog cannot also be in house 2.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     S2: dog!= 2.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     The cat is immediately to the left of the coffee, so the cat’s house index plus one equals the coffee’s house index.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     S3: cat + 1 == coffee.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     The green house appears somewhere to the left of the white house.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     S4: green < white.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     The dog is not in the first house.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     S5: Not(dog == 1).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     The cat cannot be in house 1 or house 3.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     S6: And(cat!= 1, cat!= 3).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     The milk is located either in house 1 or in house 5.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     S7: Or(milk == 1, milk == 5).
