[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "Name": ["Peter", "Eric", "Arnold"],
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "Color": ["red", "white", "yellow"],
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "Children": ["Fred", "Meredith", "Bella"]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m }
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m Correct Example Output:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m <answer>{
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "n_houses": 3,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "attribute_values": {
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "Name": ["Peter", "Eric", "Arnold"],
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "Color": ["red", "white", "yellow"],
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "Children": ["Fred", "Meredith", "Bella"]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   },
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "syntactic_clues": [
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "C1: Arnold == red.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "C2: Fred < Eric.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "C3: red == 2.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "C4: Bella == 1.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "C5: white == Meredith."
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   ],
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m   "reasoning": [
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "Clue 3 immediately anchors the red favorite color in the second house, which is a very strong positional fact to start from.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "S1: red == 2.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "Clue 1 then ties Arnold directly to the red color, so Arnold must be in that same second house."
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "S2: Arnold == red.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "Putting those two together, Arnold is fixed in house 2. At this point, house 2 is completely identified as “Arnold’s house,” and we know it has the red color.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "S3: Arnold == 2.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "Clue 4 gives us another concrete placement: the child Bella is in the first house. So whatever person lives in house 1, their child must be Bella.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "S4: Bella == 1.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "So far, we know: House 1 has child Bella, House 2 has Arnold and the color red, House 3 is still entirely open. Now we look at Clue 2, which introduces a relative ordering: the person whose child is Fred is somewhere to the left of Eric. This doesn’t give a house yet, but it constrains the ordering.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "S5: Fred < Eric.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "Since houses are only 1 through 3, Eric cannot be in the first house (there would be nothing to the left of him). That means Eric must be in house 2 or house 3.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "S6: Or(Eric == 2, Eric == 3).",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "But we already know Arnold occupies house 2, and all people are distinct. So Eric cannot be in house 2 and must therefore be in house 3.",
[36m(TaskRunner pid=344394)[0m     "S7: Eric == 3",
